WEBVTT

00:01.251 --> 00:03.835
[thunderclap]

00:03.836 --> 00:05.464
[thunder rumbling]

00:10.844 --> 00:13.055
[eerie music playing]

00:34.993 --> 00:38.705
[sighs] Come on, cancer, cancer, cancer.

00:59.518 --> 01:02.729
[mysterious music playing]

01:27.004 --> 01:28.463
- [radio crackles]
- [Patricia] Tom?

01:29.089 --> 01:30.340
Tom, can you hear me?

01:33.886 --> 01:35.470
You don't have to do this.

01:38.724 --> 01:40.141
[Wyck] Yes, you do!

01:40.142 --> 01:41.476
[Patricia] Don't listen to him.

01:45.480 --> 01:46.481
Patricia.

01:48.442 --> 01:49.443
[Patricia] Tom.

01:51.445 --> 01:52.863
Keep them in the shelter.

01:54.072 --> 01:55.741
And keep an eye on my son.

01:56.867 --> 01:58.035
[Patricia] Tom, wait.

02:32.903 --> 02:33.904
Ruth!

02:36.532 --> 02:37.533
Ruth?

02:40.452 --> 02:41.453
Ruth!

02:47.000 --> 02:48.001
Ruth?

02:53.465 --> 02:54.466
Ruth?

02:56.969 --> 02:59.972
[ominous music playing]

03:04.226 --> 03:08.355
[person straining, breathing heavily]

03:11.483 --> 03:12.484
[Tom] Ruth?

03:26.415 --> 03:28.833
[sighs, gasps] Oh, Tom.

03:28.834 --> 03:31.544
- [chuckles] Oh, you scared me.
- I'm-I'm so sorry.

03:31.545 --> 03:34.297
I… [stammers] …I tried
ringing and knocking.

03:34.298 --> 03:36.799
Oh. What are you doing here?

03:36.800 --> 03:38.385
[music playing through headphones]

03:41.013 --> 03:42.973
You came to take me to the shelter.

03:43.473 --> 03:45.934
[gasps] Oh, Tom. [chuckles]

03:46.435 --> 03:48.979
I thought you all had forgotten about me.

03:51.523 --> 03:53.275
- Never.
- I'll pack.

03:53.775 --> 03:55.611
I'll be quick. [chuckles]

03:56.195 --> 03:57.196
[sighs]

03:57.696 --> 04:01.741
Actually, um, you know,
the roads are pretty flooded right now,

04:01.742 --> 04:04.203
so may-maybe we should
just hunker down here.

04:05.579 --> 04:06.580
Well,

04:07.664 --> 04:10.667
we've weathered storms together before,
haven't we?

04:12.252 --> 04:13.253
We have.

04:14.505 --> 04:16.422
Oh! Let me get you a towel.

04:16.423 --> 04:18.590
- Oh.
- Oh, you and me both. [chuckling]

04:18.591 --> 04:21.386
I did two miles. [giggles]

04:24.598 --> 04:28.101
[eerie music playing]

04:30.771 --> 04:32.272
[thunderclap]

04:40.739 --> 04:42.741
[people chattering]

04:46.453 --> 04:48.204
[Patricia] 200 cans of water.

04:48.205 --> 04:49.623
A hundred MREs.

04:50.582 --> 04:52.292
[Wyck] How many people do we have?

04:52.918 --> 04:54.085
137.

04:54.086 --> 04:56.213
[sighs] All right.

04:56.713 --> 04:59.174
[clicks tongue]
Half-shares for kids. I can do without.

04:59.925 --> 05:03.428
- Yeah.
- Gal who had my job before me,

05:04.179 --> 05:07.266
she told me to never go into this shelter.

05:07.933 --> 05:09.643
And why would that be?

05:11.478 --> 05:12.521
She never said.

05:13.480 --> 05:16.108
Rosemary,
how's that story helpful right now?

05:16.984 --> 05:19.277
I guess we're not in the mood
for conversation.

05:19.278 --> 05:20.445
No, I guess we're not.

05:21.154 --> 05:23.739
[breathes deeply] Okay.

05:23.740 --> 05:26.368
We got a lot of people in one place.

05:27.202 --> 05:29.745
Under pressure, things turn fast.

05:29.746 --> 05:32.332
We have to keep them calm. Yeah?

05:34.126 --> 05:35.209
Yeah.

05:35.210 --> 05:37.087
[chattering continues]

05:37.963 --> 05:38.964
You hear that?

05:40.340 --> 05:41.383
Their voices.

05:41.884 --> 05:43.051
They're getting louder.

05:44.636 --> 05:46.179
[ominous music playing]

05:46.180 --> 05:49.141
[people gasping, clamoring]

05:59.651 --> 06:01.111
[Dr. Morgan humming, scatting]

06:05.073 --> 06:06.282
[Chelle clears throat]

06:06.283 --> 06:07.826
[humming, scatting continues]

06:15.000 --> 06:18.462
[Dr. Morgan] Okay. Everything looks fine.
Probably a false alarm.

06:19.838 --> 06:22.633
- Can I speak to you outside?
- Uh, yeah.

06:27.596 --> 06:28.972
The baby's coming tonight.

06:29.515 --> 06:31.599
What? No.

06:31.600 --> 06:33.810
No, no, no, no. That can't happen.

06:35.938 --> 06:38.564
[stammers] I mean, uh, that's impossible.

06:38.565 --> 06:40.399
She's not due for another seven weeks.

06:40.400 --> 06:43.612
I'm sorry. I didn't realize
you went to medical school.

06:59.044 --> 07:01.213
[Ruth] I'm worried about my herb garden.

07:03.298 --> 07:05.008
[sighs] You think it's gonna be okay?

07:06.844 --> 07:07.970
I think so.

07:09.263 --> 07:10.264
[chuckles]

07:11.807 --> 07:13.141
[Ruth] How about some tea?

07:13.642 --> 07:14.643
Please.

07:15.227 --> 07:16.395
Okay.

07:22.484 --> 07:25.070
That's a very f-full calendar.

07:26.238 --> 07:28.657
Oh, yes. I keep busy.

07:30.492 --> 07:32.035
Still very active.

07:34.037 --> 07:35.413
"Story Club"?

07:35.414 --> 07:39.041
Oh, some of us write stories
and then get together to share them.

07:39.042 --> 07:41.712
You know,
that's how Frankenstein was written.

07:43.213 --> 07:46.383
I'm no Mary Shelley of course,
but we have a lot of fun.

07:47.634 --> 07:51.221
[Tom] "Help Deirdre down.
Help Deirdre up."

07:52.139 --> 07:53.515
Who's Deirdre?

07:54.016 --> 07:55.892
You know Deirdre Kane.

07:55.893 --> 07:57.310
She's tough as nails,

07:57.311 --> 08:00.688
but she still needs help getting down
her porch every morning

08:00.689 --> 08:02.148
and then back up after lunch.

08:02.149 --> 08:04.443
Otherwise, she's stuck in there
all day long.

08:06.278 --> 08:07.863
You do that every day?

08:08.447 --> 08:10.532
Oh, it's nothing. I'm happy to do it.

08:15.787 --> 08:17.164
Can I use your bathroom?

08:18.123 --> 08:19.207
What?

08:19.208 --> 08:21.167
- Can I use your bathroom?
- Oh, sure.

08:21.168 --> 08:23.003
It's just right around here, to the right.

08:25.964 --> 08:27.758
[breathing heavily]

08:30.135 --> 08:31.719
What the fuck am I doing? We're going…

08:31.720 --> 08:34.805
- We're going off Rosemary's genealogy?
- [radio beeps]

08:34.806 --> 08:37.476
- [thunderclap]
- [Ruth yelps]

08:38.644 --> 08:40.978
- [radio beeps, distorts]
- [Patricia speaks indistinctly]

08:40.979 --> 08:44.358
- Patricia, is Evan okay? Patricia?
- [radio static]

08:45.067 --> 08:46.318
[sighs]

08:50.489 --> 08:51.490
[sighs]

09:23.230 --> 09:24.606
This should warm you up.

09:28.527 --> 09:31.029
I make my tea from my own herb garden.

09:31.530 --> 09:33.281
I made a peppermint,
which is a pick-me-up,

09:33.282 --> 09:36.868
and I made a chamomile and lavender,
which is calm and soothing.

09:36.869 --> 09:38.287
So, you pick.

09:42.207 --> 09:45.459
Let's-Let's do calm and soothing.

09:45.460 --> 09:47.296
Okay. That's nice.

09:52.509 --> 09:54.177
This one steeps for 27 minutes.

09:54.178 --> 09:56.345
What? [stammers] No, no.

09:56.346 --> 09:59.432
- Uh, how long does the other one take?
- Three minutes.

09:59.433 --> 10:01.726
Oh, let's-let's do that.

10:01.727 --> 10:03.269
But I already put this one in.

10:03.270 --> 10:04.688
Let's just do the other one.

10:07.191 --> 10:11.027
[huffs, chuckles]
I'm not gonna waste herbs, Tom.

10:11.028 --> 10:12.904
I finally got you in my house.

10:12.905 --> 10:15.072
I'm going to give you a proper tour.

10:15.073 --> 10:16.867
Come on. Come on.

10:17.451 --> 10:19.243
Don't be such a sad sack. Come on.

10:19.244 --> 10:20.953
[timer ticking]

10:20.954 --> 10:23.165
[sinister music playing]

10:34.301 --> 10:36.302
- Here you go.
- [tourist] Where's the bathroom?

10:36.303 --> 10:37.930
Bathroom is that way.

10:39.139 --> 10:40.348
Hey there, little guy.

10:40.349 --> 10:41.350
Take that.

10:42.226 --> 10:44.561
Here you go. And…

10:45.979 --> 10:47.147
[mutters]

10:51.610 --> 10:53.945
[ominous music playing]

10:53.946 --> 10:54.947
[Ray] Patricia.

10:56.365 --> 10:57.698
Uh, quick question.

10:57.699 --> 10:59.951
How much longer are we gonna be down here?

10:59.952 --> 11:02.745
- [clicks tongue] Uh… [stammers]
- [old citizen] Ash Wednesday Nor'easter

11:02.746 --> 11:05.374
of '62 lasted five days.

11:06.124 --> 11:10.044
But here, on this island,
we've had storms last twice that.

11:10.045 --> 11:11.754
[people murmuring]

11:11.755 --> 11:15.801
[smacks lips] Yeah, we have shelter,
power, plenty of food and water.

11:16.552 --> 11:18.470
We'll ride this out. Okay?

11:23.851 --> 11:25.726
Look for ways to distract people.

11:25.727 --> 11:27.729
More games, cards, anything.

11:28.355 --> 11:30.065
Games. Cards.

11:31.608 --> 11:35.070
Uh, Patty, have you seen Tom?
I really need to talk to him right now.

11:35.904 --> 11:38.448
Um, I don't know. Sorry.

11:40.617 --> 11:42.910
[tourist 1] A paramedic
was stabbed last night.

11:42.911 --> 11:44.079
[tourist 2] What?

11:51.753 --> 11:53.088
[chuckles]

11:58.927 --> 12:00.304
[whistles] Hey.

12:01.263 --> 12:03.306
- I found something.
- What?

12:03.307 --> 12:04.765
[PJ] I found a way out.

12:04.766 --> 12:05.851
- Okay.
- [PJ] Way out.

12:06.351 --> 12:09.520
- Come on. I got a joint. Let's smoke it.
- I…

12:09.521 --> 12:11.606
- Yes. Okay.
- Yeah, you can come too. Sure, come on.

12:11.607 --> 12:13.357
- Come on.
- No, I don't think…

12:13.358 --> 12:14.359
Okay.

12:15.110 --> 12:17.779
[eerie music playing]

12:21.158 --> 12:22.742
[Kelly gasps] Creepy.

12:22.743 --> 12:24.286
- [PJ] Don't fall down.
- [Evan] Mmm.

12:31.752 --> 12:33.545
[Kelly] What is this place?

12:34.796 --> 12:35.797
Can we go?

12:40.052 --> 12:41.845
Evan? Come on.

12:43.597 --> 12:45.265
- Yeah, let's do it.
- [both chuckle]

13:56.962 --> 13:59.630
[cheerful music playing on projector]

13:59.631 --> 14:02.009
So, you're an offering.

14:02.926 --> 14:05.928
You've been carefully selected
by a committee of your peers

14:05.929 --> 14:09.432
in a very fair,
very rigorous selection process.

14:09.433 --> 14:11.935
[chuckles] Maybe you've committed a crime.

14:12.519 --> 14:13.896
Or owe a debt to society.

14:14.521 --> 14:17.064
Or have been found wanting in some way.

14:17.065 --> 14:18.608
Although you'll never know,

14:18.609 --> 14:20.109
take comfort in the fact

14:20.110 --> 14:23.322
that there is an absolutely
unassailable reason you're here.

14:24.031 --> 14:26.533
Accept your fate and take pride.

14:27.367 --> 14:32.331
Your sacrifice will save countless members
of our community from needless suffering.

14:33.207 --> 14:34.833
Thank you again for your sacrifice.

14:35.459 --> 14:37.503
Widow's Bay thanks you.

14:43.717 --> 14:46.720
- [thunderclap]
- [thunder rumbling]

14:53.894 --> 14:55.771
This is where Evan stays.

14:57.940 --> 14:59.691
Picked that up at a yard sale.

15:00.484 --> 15:02.069
Boys love their cars.

15:03.278 --> 15:04.279
[Tom] Mmm.

15:06.114 --> 15:08.699
- What's that?
- [Ruth] Oh. [chuckles]

15:08.700 --> 15:12.995
He asked for an emergency ladder,
in case of fire.

15:12.996 --> 15:14.915
[chuckles] So smart.

15:15.624 --> 15:16.625
Yeah.

15:17.543 --> 15:19.919
[timer ticking]

15:19.920 --> 15:22.714
[ominous music playing]

15:26.677 --> 15:27.802
[Ruth] Oh.

15:27.803 --> 15:28.928
[smooth jazz music playing]

15:28.929 --> 15:30.472
[breathes deeply] My Alfred.

15:30.973 --> 15:32.558
I loved him so much.

15:33.141 --> 15:34.350
Old boyfriend?

15:34.351 --> 15:35.434
Yes.

15:35.435 --> 15:38.772
But he got bit by an animal
and became that animal.

15:40.315 --> 15:42.359
Oh, this was a thrill.

15:42.943 --> 15:44.027
Keith Martin.

15:45.195 --> 15:46.321
He made a pass.

15:47.197 --> 15:53.203
Oh. My first day as a secretary
to the mayor, Howard the Coward.

15:53.704 --> 15:55.205
He was a decent man.

15:55.914 --> 15:57.456
I was surprised when he left,

15:57.457 --> 15:58.584
but people get scared.

15:59.459 --> 16:00.586
He made a pass.

16:01.086 --> 16:05.047
Oh. Pastor Roberts. What a gem.

16:05.048 --> 16:06.883
He was like a father to me.

16:06.884 --> 16:09.343
- Please don't tell me he made a pass.
- [laughs]

16:09.344 --> 16:12.598
No, don't be silly. Of course… not.

16:13.098 --> 16:14.266
Oh, you know what?

16:15.100 --> 16:17.644
You're right, he did make a pass.

16:18.478 --> 16:19.605
So did she.

16:20.189 --> 16:21.773
[breathes deeply, sighs]

16:23.817 --> 16:25.484
Oh, is that… is that your parents?

16:25.485 --> 16:26.944
[Ruth] Oh, yes.

16:26.945 --> 16:28.321
Wait, is that this house?

16:28.322 --> 16:30.323
[chuckles] That's right.

16:30.324 --> 16:33.159
Yeah. My… My daddy built this house.

16:33.160 --> 16:34.161
Really?

16:34.953 --> 16:36.622
Back when they did things right.

16:37.122 --> 16:40.042
It's been through some hard times,
but it's still standing.

16:41.668 --> 16:43.378
[inhales deeply] But… [sighs]

16:44.046 --> 16:45.839
…something got Daddy in the lake.

16:46.757 --> 16:47.882
Jesus, Ruth.

16:47.883 --> 16:49.551
You've really been through it.

16:50.886 --> 16:53.638
Well, one of the benefits
of growing up in Widow's Bay

16:53.639 --> 16:56.308
is that we learn to weather the storms.

16:58.602 --> 17:01.021
It shouldn't have to be that way.

17:02.105 --> 17:03.649
It shouldn't, but it is.

17:04.148 --> 17:05.692
There's no way around it.

17:08.987 --> 17:10.113
What if there was?

17:13.200 --> 17:14.201
How do you mean?

17:17.579 --> 17:18.871
I-I-I don't know.

17:18.872 --> 17:20.207
I mean, what… what if, um…

17:23.460 --> 17:26.963
What if there was something
that you could do to change things?

17:26.964 --> 17:30.259
What-What would you be willing
to do for that?

17:33.679 --> 17:35.722
[inhales deeply]
Have you ever heard of the…

17:36.306 --> 17:37.599
the trolley problem?

17:38.100 --> 17:43.021
You mean back in '42 when we tried to
build one and all the workers disappeared?

17:44.314 --> 17:46.482
No. What? No. No.

17:46.483 --> 17:50.528
So… [stammers]
…imagine there's a runaway trolley

17:50.529 --> 17:52.822
and-and it's barreling down the tracks

17:52.823 --> 17:55.366
and it's gonna plow through a-a-a crowd.

17:55.367 --> 17:56.785
A big crowd of people.

17:57.911 --> 17:59.745
Now, there's a lever that you can pull

17:59.746 --> 18:04.168
that'll divert it to a different track,
where it will only hit one person.

18:06.295 --> 18:08.463
Would you… Would you pull the lever?

18:10.299 --> 18:13.301
Oh, I get it.
And then all those people would be saved?

18:13.302 --> 18:15.137
Yes. Yes, exactly.

18:15.721 --> 18:17.347
Well, I wouldn't pull the lever.

18:18.015 --> 18:20.266
- But-But you'd have to.
- So I don't have a choice?

18:20.267 --> 18:23.145
- Then what's the question?
- No. I mean, yes. You have a choice.

18:24.479 --> 18:25.772
Um. But…

18:26.356 --> 18:28.566
But not a real one,
because if you don't pull that lever,

18:28.567 --> 18:29.568
all those people will die.

18:30.611 --> 18:33.030
- Well, I wouldn't pull it.
- How could you not pull it?

18:34.823 --> 18:38.160
[sighs] The runaway trolley is life.

18:39.828 --> 18:41.163
The lever is me.

18:41.914 --> 18:47.544
You can't control the bad things
that happen in life, Tom.

18:48.545 --> 18:50.755
But if I pull that lever, it's a choice,

18:50.756 --> 18:53.216
and I'm choosing to kill that person,

18:53.217 --> 18:54.801
and I could never do that.

18:56.428 --> 18:58.222
There-There's a quote I love.

18:59.097 --> 19:00.974
I've got it up here in cross stitch.

19:05.270 --> 19:06.939
So, I'm gonna read it to you.

19:08.232 --> 19:09.233
[clears throat]

19:10.692 --> 19:14.655
"The world is violent and mercurial.

19:15.489 --> 19:17.574
It will have its way with you."

19:20.244 --> 19:22.662
Can't read that. I can't read that part.

19:22.663 --> 19:25.123
Can't… Can't read…
Oh, here. Here it is. Wait.

19:26.625 --> 19:31.213
"We live in a perpetually
burning building,

19:32.506 --> 19:39.471
and what we must save from it
all the time is love."

19:41.098 --> 19:43.267
[sighs] Tennessee Williams.

19:46.144 --> 19:48.312
Well, let him spend the night at our Inn,

19:48.313 --> 19:51.483
and then he'll see how good
he's got it in the burning building.

19:54.152 --> 19:55.404
Come on, Ruth.

19:57.239 --> 19:59.115
This place is a house of horrors.

19:59.116 --> 20:02.244
[chuckles] Life is a house of horrors.

20:02.828 --> 20:05.163
You should know that
better than anyone, Tom.

20:07.374 --> 20:09.209
I've always worried about you.

20:09.793 --> 20:12.670
You've-You've worried about me?

20:12.671 --> 20:13.754
Why?

20:13.755 --> 20:15.382
You avoid the truth.

20:16.383 --> 20:19.386
I mean, you want this
to be Martha's Vineyard.

20:19.970 --> 20:21.305
It's never gonna be.

20:21.889 --> 20:24.557
There's no bliss
waiting at the finish line.

20:24.558 --> 20:27.101
Even if there was,
it would just be taken away from you

20:27.102 --> 20:29.103
because that's just life.

20:29.104 --> 20:32.190
In all its ugly,
beautiful, terrible glory.

20:32.191 --> 20:33.233
You just…

20:33.817 --> 20:35.736
You just have to accept it.

20:46.914 --> 20:47.998
[Ruth sighs]

20:49.958 --> 20:51.460
- [thunderclap]
- [thunder rumbling]

20:56.757 --> 20:59.885
[suspenseful music playing]

21:05.015 --> 21:06.099
[Tom] Ruth?

21:08.769 --> 21:10.062
Where did you find this?

21:13.357 --> 21:15.984
This was passed down to me.
It's a family heirloom.

21:18.612 --> 21:19.613
Isn't it lovely?

21:22.699 --> 21:24.326
It looks beautiful on you.

21:25.536 --> 21:26.537
Thank you.

21:28.163 --> 21:29.164
[timer dings]

21:33.710 --> 21:34.753
I'll get it.

21:37.923 --> 21:40.676
- [thuds]
- [crushing object]

21:55.816 --> 21:57.651
[thunder rumbling]

22:11.790 --> 22:13.292
[thunderclap]

22:15.169 --> 22:17.671
[ominous music playing]

22:30.184 --> 22:31.435
[Patricia sighs] Who's next?

22:32.186 --> 22:33.769
Eve. Okay.

22:33.770 --> 22:34.854
There you go.

22:34.855 --> 22:36.689
- Have a nice meal.
- [citizen] Thank you.

22:36.690 --> 22:38.774
- Thank you. What's your name? Todd?
- Yes.

22:38.775 --> 22:40.152
[Patricia] Have we got a Todd?

22:40.777 --> 22:43.988
[stammers] W-What is he getting?
A car loan? Let's go. Here.

22:43.989 --> 22:45.823
- Um. Hey…
- Yeah, Tom.

22:45.824 --> 22:48.034
- Um, yes, we met yesterday. Thank you.
- Yes, Tom.

22:48.035 --> 22:51.037
Geez. People are really… [huffs] …rude.

22:51.038 --> 22:54.208
Jesus Christ.
You gotta be fucking kidding me.

22:54.791 --> 22:57.001
- This is covered in mold, everyone.
- [all clamoring]

22:57.002 --> 22:58.461
Okay. Well, let us…

22:58.462 --> 23:01.215
- W-We'll get you another--
- Mine are bad too. And-And the water.

23:01.798 --> 23:04.509
Okay. Well, we'll, um, sort through these

23:04.510 --> 23:06.093
- and, um--
- Mine are fine.

23:06.094 --> 23:07.804
- [clamoring stops]
- Huh?

23:09.139 --> 23:10.932
- Bro, give me your--
- No, no, no! Hey!

23:10.933 --> 23:12.016
[clamoring resumes]

23:12.017 --> 23:14.060
Whoa! Hey! Hey!

23:14.061 --> 23:15.686
Excuse me. Hey, hey, you.

23:15.687 --> 23:18.523
I want his stash. I want his stash.

23:18.524 --> 23:20.525
- Hey. Don't hit him!
- Hey. Ow!

23:20.526 --> 23:24.278
What the fuck are we supposed to do
about food around here?

23:24.279 --> 23:27.281
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa! Hey!
We're gonna s… Whoa!

23:27.282 --> 23:29.283
- [clamoring stops]
- We're gonna sort it all out, people.

23:29.284 --> 23:31.827
Don't worry, just be calm, all right?

23:31.828 --> 23:33.080
[old citizen] He's right.

23:34.414 --> 23:36.708
We can go weeks without food.

23:38.877 --> 23:40.461
But not without water.

23:40.462 --> 23:41.629
[Wyck] Oh, fucking Christ.

23:41.630 --> 23:43.673
That's what we're saying.
We need some fucking water.

23:43.674 --> 23:45.174
[clamoring resumes]

23:45.175 --> 23:47.177
[tourist] The hell is wrong
with this island?

23:51.265 --> 23:52.266
[Chelle] Hey.

23:59.314 --> 24:00.732
You know what I think?

24:02.484 --> 24:05.945
I think that this is gonna be
a funny story we tell our kid some day.

24:05.946 --> 24:10.158
[chuckles] Being born
on some crazy island shelter.

24:10.784 --> 24:12.786
With all these crazy people.

24:13.745 --> 24:15.873
[chuckles]

24:17.416 --> 24:18.541
[clicks tongue] Oh.

24:18.542 --> 24:19.834
[clears throat]

24:19.835 --> 24:21.419
[inhales sharply]

24:21.420 --> 24:23.797
[moaning]

24:26.175 --> 24:28.677
[people clamoring]

24:37.352 --> 24:38.353
[sighs]

24:40.230 --> 24:41.231
I need water

24:42.191 --> 24:43.482
for my wife.

24:43.483 --> 24:45.484
I saved these two for you.

24:45.485 --> 24:46.486
[clears throat]

24:50.574 --> 24:51.575
Thanks.

24:53.911 --> 24:56.037
What the hell is going on down here?

24:56.038 --> 24:57.955
And how is Loftis not here?

24:57.956 --> 24:58.957
[Rosemary] Who knows?

24:59.541 --> 25:00.876
Something's off though.

25:01.376 --> 25:02.377
What?

25:03.170 --> 25:05.713
Had me do a whole genealogy on Ruth.

25:05.714 --> 25:07.590
Do you know how long that took?

25:07.591 --> 25:11.637
Then the three of them huddle up
and whisper like little schoolgirls.

25:12.221 --> 25:13.680
Didn't include me.

25:14.306 --> 25:16.058
Guess I'll go fuck myself.

25:22.689 --> 25:23.732
Patricia.

25:24.900 --> 25:26.235
What the hell is going on?

25:27.861 --> 25:29.071
Patricia.

25:36.995 --> 25:38.539
What is Loftis doing?

25:47.381 --> 25:50.717
Barricade this door and don't
let anyone in till I get back.

25:51.510 --> 25:53.594
[Chelle] Honey? Honey, w-what's going on?

25:53.595 --> 25:55.012
Uh, I'll be right back.

25:55.013 --> 25:57.682
- What? What are you talking about?
- I just have something I need to do.

25:57.683 --> 25:59.643
[Chelle] No. Lis… Listen to me. Bechir.

26:01.311 --> 26:03.397
[thunder rumbling]

26:11.864 --> 26:13.448
[thunderclap]

26:36.805 --> 26:40.016
When Lauren died, I didn't know…

26:40.017 --> 26:41.977
I didn't know what
I was gonna do with myself.

26:45.606 --> 26:48.399
You know she tried to talk to me about it?

26:48.400 --> 26:50.319
The island. And, um…

26:55.490 --> 26:56.949
I laughed it off.

26:56.950 --> 26:57.951
[sniffles]

26:58.827 --> 27:00.204
I teased her about it.

27:03.999 --> 27:08.128
I don't understand why
I didn't just listen.

27:12.341 --> 27:15.844
And after that ferry ride,
when they told me it was a stroke…

27:17.346 --> 27:18.597
I-I knew…

27:22.684 --> 27:26.104
I knew and I still brought tourists here.

27:29.316 --> 27:31.318
[stammers] Because I wanted more for him…

27:33.445 --> 27:34.613
And myself.

27:37.741 --> 27:40.160
And now I've put
all these people in danger.

27:44.248 --> 27:46.625
There are families in the shelters.

27:48.210 --> 27:49.586
I have families that…

27:51.755 --> 27:53.215
I've brought here.

27:54.341 --> 27:57.594
[inhales deeply, sighs]

28:09.565 --> 28:10.732
I'm sorry.

28:15.654 --> 28:17.531
But I had to make it right.

28:30.419 --> 28:31.628
[exhales deeply]

29:02.284 --> 29:03.492
- [inhales sharply]
- [gasps]

29:03.493 --> 29:05.078
Whoo!

29:06.872 --> 29:07.956
Where was I?

29:10.167 --> 29:14.838
Oh. That was the summer
my Aunt Betty stopped speaking.

29:15.964 --> 29:17.590
First we thought she was pouting,

29:17.591 --> 29:19.967
but then it turns out
it was something else.

29:19.968 --> 29:22.971
[thunder rumbling]

29:24.765 --> 29:29.770
[ominous music playing]

29:38.195 --> 29:39.196
Whoa.

29:40.030 --> 29:41.031
[stammers] PJ!

29:44.201 --> 29:45.744
Guys, check this shit out.

29:46.495 --> 29:50.081
[PJ] Oh, dude, come here. [chuckles]
Look at this shit.

29:50.082 --> 29:53.418
Can you believe this?
I've never heard anyone talk about…

29:55.796 --> 29:57.548
[both chuckling]

29:58.465 --> 29:59.466
[Kelly] Come on.

29:59.967 --> 30:01.718
[PJ] Yo, guys, there's another door.

30:02.386 --> 30:03.720
Come here. Check this out.

30:10.018 --> 30:11.520
- [PJ] Whoa.
- [Kelly chuckles]

30:12.062 --> 30:13.312
[PJ] Kelly, sit in the chair.

30:13.313 --> 30:15.106
[Kelly] Dude, I can't.

30:15.107 --> 30:16.899
[PJ] I think you actually have to.

30:16.900 --> 30:18.277
[Kelly chuckles] Dude.

30:19.278 --> 30:22.364
Oh, my God. This is so weird. [chuckles]

30:22.865 --> 30:24.867
This is not right.

30:25.367 --> 30:27.578
Wait. What is this?

30:28.871 --> 30:31.622
[inn guest] At this point, I'd prefer
to be out there. I really would.

30:31.623 --> 30:34.750
It's in our best interest to
stay inside until the storm passes.

30:34.751 --> 30:37.378
- But why is the door locked?
- No reason for that door to be locked.

30:37.379 --> 30:40.298
You don't have the authority
to keep us in here.

30:40.299 --> 30:42.718
- [Wyck] Keep your voice down. Hey!
- [clamoring]

30:47.848 --> 30:49.141
[Patricia] Sorry. Sorry.

30:49.641 --> 30:51.143
Just stay where you are!

30:52.519 --> 30:54.896
Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

30:54.897 --> 30:56.814
- Keep your voices down.
- [automated voice] It's time.

30:56.815 --> 30:58.733
- It's okay. Everything's okay.
- It's time.

30:58.734 --> 31:02.028
It's time. It's time.

31:02.029 --> 31:03.739
Listen to your facilitator.

31:04.323 --> 31:06.199
Move forward.

31:06.200 --> 31:08.785
- Do not beg.
- [person 1] What?

31:11.663 --> 31:14.123
- [clamoring]
- [person 2] What the fuck?

31:14.124 --> 31:16.793
That's probably what she meant. [groans]

31:18.712 --> 31:21.297
[person on recording]
Be strong. Honor the pact.

31:21.298 --> 31:24.843
And remember,
their sacrifice is our survival.

31:26.011 --> 31:30.474
The bad times will not end until the
covenant is honored, and honored fully.

31:31.058 --> 31:32.351
Life for life.

31:32.935 --> 31:35.186
The island will make its needs known.

31:35.187 --> 31:37.689
One soul for each bell toll.

31:38.482 --> 31:40.441
You will be tempted to comfort them.

31:40.442 --> 31:41.609
Do not.

31:41.610 --> 31:43.695
Their fear is necessary.

31:44.571 --> 31:46.365
They say It likes the taste.

31:47.157 --> 31:51.995
Now, let's pray for
a long and peaceful slumber.

31:55.958 --> 31:59.377
[foreboding music playing]

31:59.378 --> 32:03.798
[people in shelter clamoring]

32:03.799 --> 32:07.510
Whoa! Nobody panic.
Nobody move, it's okay.

32:07.511 --> 32:08.594
It's all right.

32:08.595 --> 32:10.012
It's okay.

32:10.013 --> 32:12.140
[people in shelter gasping, shrieking]

32:13.600 --> 32:16.352
- [Patricia] Just stay where you are!
- [Wyck] Don't move!

32:16.353 --> 32:17.854
[people shriek]

32:17.855 --> 32:19.523
Whoa, sorry. It's fine.

32:20.232 --> 32:22.359
[pants] It's all right.

32:23.485 --> 32:24.778
We're all okay.

32:26.738 --> 32:27.781
We're just…

32:28.991 --> 32:31.660
- We're just gonna ride this out together.
- [Wyck] Yeah.

32:33.370 --> 32:34.787
I know we're all scared.

32:34.788 --> 32:36.998
But we have each other.

32:36.999 --> 32:38.667
- [Wyck] Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.
- Don't we?

32:40.127 --> 32:41.795
[Patricia] Yeah? We're in it together?

32:43.297 --> 32:46.049
Okay. [chuckles] Okay.

32:50.179 --> 32:51.304
Dale?

32:51.305 --> 32:52.597
This place is…

32:52.598 --> 32:54.808
[breathes shakily, stammers]

32:56.602 --> 32:58.145
Dale, you're freaking people out.

32:59.855 --> 33:01.814
This place is a death trap!

33:01.815 --> 33:03.024
Run!

33:03.025 --> 33:04.525
[people screaming, clamoring]

33:04.526 --> 33:06.152
Run for your lives!

33:06.153 --> 33:08.447
[shouting indistinctly]

33:10.407 --> 33:11.575
[Tom] Patricia.

33:12.826 --> 33:14.493
[stammers] Patricia, she, uh…

33:14.494 --> 33:15.871
She's… She's not going.

33:27.508 --> 33:30.719
Can you please just
tell me that Evan is okay?

33:31.303 --> 33:33.305
[suspenseful music playing]

33:38.977 --> 33:40.771
[feedback from radio]

33:41.313 --> 33:44.233
- Patricia?
- [people in shelter screaming]

33:46.401 --> 33:48.486
- What's happening?
- [screaming on radio]

33:48.487 --> 33:50.071
What… What's happening?

33:50.072 --> 33:51.572
Patricia, what's happening?

33:51.573 --> 33:54.117
[screaming continues]

33:57.329 --> 34:00.457
[thunder rumbling]

34:33.156 --> 34:35.033
[snoring]

34:56.554 --> 34:58.264
[Ruth yawns]

34:58.265 --> 35:00.058
You're a good person.

35:02.186 --> 35:04.188
- Hmm.
- You don't deserve this.

35:08.275 --> 35:09.651
You know…

35:11.069 --> 35:14.072
I had an affair with a married man.

35:14.740 --> 35:15.866
[chuckles]

35:18.827 --> 35:20.078
That's okay.

35:21.038 --> 35:22.915
I was young. [inhales sharply]

35:24.041 --> 35:26.876
[chuckles] That's not true, I was 40.

35:26.877 --> 35:28.920
[chuckles]

35:28.921 --> 35:32.466
I'd love to tell you I didn't know
he was married, but I did.

35:34.635 --> 35:37.721
I wanted him to leave his wife,
but he wouldn't.

35:39.723 --> 35:41.225
I got pregnant.

35:42.392 --> 35:43.810
I hid it. [sighs]

35:45.145 --> 35:48.023
I just was not in a good place.

35:48.899 --> 35:50.650
- [exhales deeply]
- I cried.

35:50.651 --> 35:51.984
Oh, how I cried.

35:51.985 --> 35:53.529
I cried all the time.

35:55.489 --> 35:57.366
So, I gave her to him.

35:58.283 --> 36:01.577
To raise with his wife as their own.

36:01.578 --> 36:03.079
[breathes deeply]

36:03.080 --> 36:06.083
I watched my baby girl grow up from afar.

36:08.752 --> 36:10.671
She had a nice childhood.

36:12.339 --> 36:13.715
They loved her.

36:15.926 --> 36:17.010
Who?

36:17.636 --> 36:18.846
She died.

36:21.682 --> 36:24.017
But I watched her first dance.

36:24.685 --> 36:27.354
I saw her drive her first car.

36:28.689 --> 36:34.152
I saw her work her first job
serving soft-served ice cream.

36:38.115 --> 36:43.412
And I got to watch her
fall in love with you, Tom.

36:44.454 --> 36:46.330
[sinister music plays]

36:46.331 --> 36:47.332
What?

36:48.458 --> 36:50.419
My baby girl, Lauren.

36:52.045 --> 36:53.380
Your wife.

36:57.676 --> 36:59.511
You're not making any sense.

37:00.304 --> 37:03.348
I felt so awful after the ferry.

37:05.017 --> 37:08.686
I visited her at Old Home
as often as I could.

37:08.687 --> 37:11.648
I told her I was her secret mommy.

37:14.776 --> 37:16.444
No. No, I…

37:16.445 --> 37:17.738
I d… I don't believe you.

37:18.405 --> 37:21.700
Why do you think I still come in to work?

37:22.993 --> 37:25.369
I'm 84 years old, Tom.

37:25.370 --> 37:26.663
I'm tired.

37:27.831 --> 37:33.795
I come in to still be
a part of my grandson's life.

37:34.463 --> 37:35.964
[gasps]

37:36.757 --> 37:41.677
It feels so good to
finally say all this out loud.

37:41.678 --> 37:43.054
No. No, no. No, no.

37:43.055 --> 37:44.889
- To unburden myself…
- No, no. There's no way.

37:44.890 --> 37:46.474
- …after all these years.
- There's no way.

37:46.475 --> 37:49.685
- You're… You're out of your mind.
- I don't know why I chose tonight.

37:49.686 --> 37:50.896
Oh, my God.

37:53.273 --> 37:56.151
Pull-out method just doesn't work.

37:56.944 --> 37:58.111
- No!
- Oh.

37:58.654 --> 38:00.112
Who else have you told, Ruth?

38:00.113 --> 38:01.614
No one, Tom! No one!

38:01.615 --> 38:03.700
[sobs] No one, no one.

38:08.038 --> 38:09.206
Oh, my God.

38:14.211 --> 38:16.213
He's never gonna leave the island.

38:20.050 --> 38:23.011
[Tom breathes shakily]

38:34.189 --> 38:35.566
[exhales deeply]

38:38.360 --> 38:39.694
Oh, Ruth.

38:39.695 --> 38:41.362
I have to get you to a doctor.

38:41.363 --> 38:42.572
[Ruth groans]

38:42.573 --> 38:44.156
Hold tight. Ready?

38:44.157 --> 38:46.743
One, two, three. [grunts]

38:54.209 --> 38:55.586
[door creaks]

38:58.589 --> 38:59.965
- No!
- [gunshot]

39:00.924 --> 39:02.009
[Ruth's body thuds]

39:04.011 --> 39:05.179
[gasps]

39:10.893 --> 39:12.186
What did you do?

39:13.687 --> 39:15.646
I won't damn my child.

39:15.647 --> 39:18.691
No. No, no, no, no, no.

39:18.692 --> 39:21.361
- Ruth?
- Patricia said you'd be ending it but…

39:22.112 --> 39:23.863
- Hey, I knew--
- She's not the last.

39:23.864 --> 39:24.947
I-I knew you wouldn't.

39:24.948 --> 39:26.450
She's not the last descendant!

39:33.373 --> 39:34.374
What?

39:41.423 --> 39:42.674
Then who?

39:44.051 --> 39:45.093
Who, Tom?

39:49.139 --> 39:50.389
- [thunderclaps]
- Who?

39:50.390 --> 39:52.683
Okay. Bechir, put it down.

39:52.684 --> 39:54.602
Please, please p-put it down.

39:54.603 --> 39:56.355
Put the gun down.

39:58.273 --> 40:03.028
Look, my child is about to be
born and I just need to know who.

40:04.238 --> 40:05.989
[stammers] I-I don't know.

40:08.867 --> 40:10.409
[Kelly] Wait, what is this thing?

40:10.410 --> 40:12.161
[PJ] Stick it in your eye
and it keeps it open…

40:12.162 --> 40:13.746
[Kelly] You know what?
You get in the chair.

40:13.747 --> 40:15.665
- [PJ] Strap me into it.
- [Kelly] For real?

40:15.666 --> 40:17.376
- [PJ] Yeah.
- [Kelly] Okay.

40:19.044 --> 40:20.336
[screams]

40:20.337 --> 40:21.671
- PJ!
- [laughs]

40:21.672 --> 40:22.756
- You're insane.
- [Kenny] Hey!

40:23.674 --> 40:29.429
PJ Glanville, get your ass
out of that weird fucking chair.

40:32.766 --> 40:35.184
- Now!
- [PJ] Okay. I'm trying to.

40:35.185 --> 40:36.435
- [Kenny] Come on.
- [Kelly] Sorry.

40:36.436 --> 40:37.479
[Evan] Sorry.

40:38.105 --> 40:39.314
Get outta here.

40:44.903 --> 40:46.821
- [Kenny] Whoa. Open up!
- [Evan] The fuck? Come on.

40:46.822 --> 40:48.447
- It's locked.
- [Kenny] Open this door now!

40:48.448 --> 40:49.782
- Go. Go, go, go!
- [Kelly] Wait!

40:49.783 --> 40:51.368
- [Kenny] Open up!
- Guys! Guys! What…

40:54.079 --> 40:56.164
- [Kenny] Something's happening.
- It's locked!

40:57.040 --> 40:58.917
- [Kenny] Open the door!
- I'm-I'm trying!

40:59.418 --> 41:01.170
- [Kenny] Oh, God. Oh, God!
- [grunts]

41:02.296 --> 41:04.298
[Kenny screams]

41:06.758 --> 41:09.761
[breathes shakily]

41:10.679 --> 41:12.930
[Bechir] You are always lying.

41:12.931 --> 41:15.516
[thunder rumbling]

41:15.517 --> 41:18.020
[thunder, wind fades]

41:25.944 --> 41:27.112
It stopped.

41:34.620 --> 41:35.746
Why did it stop?

41:40.250 --> 41:41.459
[Tom] Ruth.

41:41.460 --> 41:43.377
Ruth? Ruth? [breathing shakily]

41:43.378 --> 41:44.963
Oh, fuck. [sniffles]

41:54.473 --> 41:55.724
Tom?

41:56.767 --> 41:59.060
[sniffles] Will you fucking help me?

41:59.061 --> 42:00.436
We need to get her to a doctor.

42:00.437 --> 42:04.274
- Ruth. Talk to me.
- Why did it stop?

42:06.068 --> 42:09.404
- [person 1] Whoa.
- [people chattering]

42:18.413 --> 42:20.999
You're okay. You're okay.
You're okay. Stay there.

42:24.670 --> 42:26.213
[door unlocks]

42:54.783 --> 42:56.076
He must've done it.

43:09.882 --> 43:12.134
[door creaks, unlocks]

43:25.480 --> 43:27.441
[Evan breathes shakily]

43:40.120 --> 43:43.123
[breathes shakily]

45:29.605 --> 45:36.278
[eight bell tolls]

45:41.950 --> 45:43.452
[bell tolling stops]

45:45.871 --> 45:47.873
[suspenseful music playing]
